---
import ToolPage from '../../layouts/ToolPage.astro';
import CommandSandbox from '../../components/viz/CommandSandbox.tsx';
import PyPad from '../../components/viz/PyPad.tsx';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
---

<ToolPage figure="terminal" title="Sandbox" lede="Type the commands the tools use and see what they print, or run real Python for the arithmetic behind model sizes.">
  <CommandSandbox client:visible />
  <PyPad client:visible />
  <Fragment slot="notes">
    <h2>What is real and what is recorded</h2>
    <p>The terminal cannot run Ollama, vLLM or the Hugging Face CLI in a web page. It replays example output, so you can learn what each command prints and what to look for. The Python pad is real: it runs in your browser through Pyodide.</p>
    <p>To run the tools for real, install them on your own machine and try the same commands. Start with <a href={withBase('/learn/local/run-models-locally/')}>Run models locally</a>.</p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolPage>
